# Shell scripts must stay LF — a shebang line with a trailing CRLF becomes
# `#!/bin/bash\r`, which the kernel can't find as an interpreter
# ("bad interpreter: No such file or directory"). Hit this for real
# building docker-entrypoint.sh locally on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# (2026-08-11, Tekniska) — the committed blob was already LF-only, so this
# doesn't rewrite anything, it just stops the same false alarm recurring
# for the next Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
